{"purpose":"Establish the product intent of the EKA ecosystem — why it exists and what it aims to become.","content":"EKA (Engineering Knowledge Architecture) is a standard for engineering knowledge: a canonical model for how knowledge is identified, structured, exchanged, and operated — together with its reference implementation (a Go library), a command-line tool, and an AI-agent integration layer. The vision is engineering knowledge that survives changes in storage, tooling, and organization, and moves losslessly between systems. It resolves three persistent problems: identity instability (knowledge addressed by location, not identity), implicit or duplicated state, and the inability to move knowledge between systems."}